id: pm-eswzn9
title: Support safe Bash completion inside quoted and escaped prefixes
description: "Extend the conservative literal matcher with an explicit Readline insertion-context contract for single quotes, double quotes and escaped prefixes. Preserve accepted argument bytes without shell evaluation on Bash 3.2 and current Bash, including candidates with Unicode, apostrophes and shell metacharacters."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-20T14:22:39.461Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-24T00:52:09.838Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-24T00:52:09.010Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-24T00:52:09.010Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Real Tab-and-Enter acceptance across quoting contexts preserves exact argument bytes; adversarial candidates cannot execute or expand globs; no global Readline option changes; current safe unquoted completion remains compatible.
parent: pm-7hx6
resolution: "Decode the current Readline word without evaluation and encode matches for single-quoted, double-quoted, and escaped insertion contexts; retain conservative refusal for ambiguous mixed segments."
expected_result: Tab completion preserves candidate argument bytes and cannot execute candidate shell syntax.
actual_result: "92 focused Bash security tests and 9,245 full coverage tests passed with 100/100/100/100 source coverage; temporary packed npm install and Node/Bun/npx/bunx smoke passed."
