comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-20T14:22:39.461Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: inspected the full all-status title census and open/in-progress inventories; Readline keyword search returned six unrelated historical items; completion history and current portability work contain no existing quoted-prefix implementation owner. This is an unclaimed UX follow-up for the deliberately conservative quoted-prefix boundary."
  "2026-09-24T00:13:27.755Z","harness:codex","TDD and native acceptance: the new quoted-prefix test failed before the implementation. The focused suite now passes 92/92; interactive Bash Tab-and-Enter in a temporary pseudo terminal preserves exact argument bytes for single-quoted, double-quoted, and escaped prefixes, including apostrophes, double quotes, dollar signs, command-substitution syntax, backticks, glob stars, exclamation marks, backslashes, and Unicode. The command-substitution sentinel remains absent. Existing unquoted data-boundary cases remain green."
  "2026-09-24T00:50:36.365Z","harness:codex","Evidence: full sandbox coverage passed 732 test files and 9,245 tests (one file and two tests skipped), with 100% statements 65,050/65,050, branches 49,672/49,672, functions 13,487/13,487, and lines 62,202/62,202. Packed npm artifact installed in an isolated temporary project; init, guide-shell package installation, Bash completion generation/bash -n, create/get, Node, Bun, offline npx, and local bunx all passed at 2026.9.23. Focused interactive pseudo-terminal completion suite passed 92/92."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-24T00:13:26.413Z","harness:codex","Bash Readline completes a replacement word, not a dequoted value. The generated matcher decodes only COMP_WORDS[COMP_CWORD] without eval, then emits syntax for the open quote mode. Raw Readline filename quoting is unsafe for dollars and backticks. A literal exclamation mark in double quotes needs a single-quoted segment because backslash-exclamation retains the slash in accepted bytes."
